# Auto-apply manifest — migrations the deploy workflow runs automatically.
#
# The deploy job (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) applies each file listed here
# during the EXPAND phase — after the new images are pulled but BEFORE the
# rolling container swap — using a one-off container from the freshly-pulled
# api image. This lands additive/idempotent schema + data changes ahead of the
# new code, so the still-running old containers keep serving and the new code
# never hits a missing column. Applied files are recorded in the
# `_manual_migrations` table, so each runs exactly once (and re-deploys skip
# them); the SQL is idempotent anyway as defence in depth.
#
# ONLY list migrations that are:
#   - additive / backward-compatible (an EXPAND migration — old code tolerates
#     it), and
#   - idempotent + safe to re-run.
# Anything destructive, or a CONTRACT step that removes a column still read by
# the currently-running code, must NOT go here — apply those by hand via the
# "Apply prod migration" workflow (apply-migration.yml) at the right moment.
#
# Order matters: files run top-to-bottom. Blank lines and #comments are ignored.

2026-07-24_account_deletion_pending.sql
2026-07-24_content_contact_details.sql
2026-07-28_review_title.sql
2026-09-01_order_delivery_address_snapshot.sql
